* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Every tracked .csv here is stored CRLF today — all 9 of them, including
# data/canada-disposal-facilities.csv and data/western-canada-facilities.csv,
# which the application reads. The blanket `eol=lf` above would convert them on
# the next renormalize, so they are excluded from conversion entirely.
#
# `-text`, not `text eol=crlf`: the latter still normalizes the *stored* blob to
# LF and only restores CRLF on checkout, so it rewrites all 9 files in history
# (measured: 5438 lines) while leaving the working tree looking unchanged.
# `-text` stores the bytes exactly as they are. Revisit in a dedicated change if
# these files should become LF; it should not ride along with a scaffolding commit.
*.csv -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
